1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
Navigation, and site settings.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:06,856
There is an About page and a journal,

3
00:00:06,856 --> 00:00:12,478
and the only way to reach either of them is the list at the bottom of the homepage.

4
00:00:12,478 --> 00:00:17,694
And the footer says Studio, because somebody typed that word into a template.

5
00:00:17,694 --> 00:00:21,216
Today, a real menu, and details the client can edit.

6
00:00:22,016 --> 00:00:25,847
There is no menu model here, and no hard coded links.

7
00:00:25,847 --> 00:00:31,847
The menu is simply the children of the site's root page that are live and marked as

8
00:00:31,847 --> 00:00:32,425
in menu.

9
00:00:32,425 --> 00:00:36,834
So an editor adds a page to the menu by ticking one checkbox,

10
00:00:36,834 --> 00:00:38,786
on that page's Promote tab.

11
00:00:39,586 --> 00:00:41,453
It is an inclusion tag.

12
00:00:41,453 --> 00:00:46,891
It finds the site for this request, takes the root page's children,

13
00:00:46,891 --> 00:00:49,651
and works out which one is active.

14
00:00:49,651 --> 00:00:52,492
Then base.html just says main menu.

15
00:00:53,292 --> 00:00:55,250
Reload the page, and.

16
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:57,301
Template syntax error.

17
00:00:57,301 --> 00:01:01,776
Navigation tags is not a registered tag library.

18
00:01:01,776 --> 00:01:04,014
And the code is correct.

19
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:10,222
The development server had already reloaded itself for the models change a minute

20
00:01:10,222 --> 00:01:10,756
earlier.

21
00:01:10,756 --> 00:01:14,896
But the reloader only watches files that are already imported,

22
00:01:14,896 --> 00:01:18,034
and a brand new tag library is not one of them.

23
00:01:18,034 --> 00:01:23,576
So any time you add a new template tags module, stop the server and start it again.

24
00:01:24,376 --> 00:01:27,233
Restarted, and now the menu is empty.

25
00:01:27,233 --> 00:01:28,855
Nothing there at all.

26
00:01:28,855 --> 00:01:33,721
Because every page on this site has show in menus set to false.

27
00:01:33,721 --> 00:01:36,810
That is the default for every page type.

28
00:01:36,810 --> 00:01:42,370
Tick the box on About and on the journal, publish, and the menu appears.

29
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:45,908
And to stop that happening next time,

30
00:01:45,908 --> 00:01:51,383
set show in menus default to true on the page types that belong in a menu.

31
00:01:51,383 --> 00:01:53,307
But be clear what it does.

32
00:01:53,307 --> 00:01:55,970
New pages start with the box ticked.

33
00:01:55,970 --> 00:01:59,004
Pages that already exist are not touched.

34
00:01:59,804 --> 00:02:03,507
The active item is a prefix match on the URL path.

35
00:02:03,507 --> 00:02:08,099
So when you are reading a post, which lives under the journal,

36
00:02:08,099 --> 00:02:10,321
the journal stays highlighted.

37
00:02:10,321 --> 00:02:13,358
And because a URL path always ends in a/,

38
00:02:13,358 --> 00:02:17,654
About can never accidentally match a page called About us.

39
00:02:18,454 --> 00:02:19,764
And it is cheap.

40
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:23,612
I rendered the menu tag on its own and counted.

41
00:02:23,612 --> 00:02:25,168
One database query.

42
00:02:25,168 --> 00:02:26,642
No caching needed.

43
00:02:26,642 --> 00:02:33,520
That changes once you build dropdowns, because each level is another query per item.

44
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,481
Now the footer.

45
00:02:35,481 --> 00:02:39,431
Wagtail's settings app, plus its context processor,

46
00:02:39,431 --> 00:02:44,154
and every template on the site can read the studio's details.

47
00:02:44,954 --> 00:02:49,322
A settings model is a normal Django model with one decorator.

48
00:02:49,322 --> 00:02:54,048
Site setting, rather than generic setting, means one row per site,

49
00:02:54,048 --> 00:02:59,276
so if this install ever runs a second site, it gets its own phone number.

50
00:03:00,076 --> 00:03:01,201
And watch this.

51
00:03:01,201 --> 00:03:03,226
No rows before any request.

52
00:03:03,226 --> 00:03:05,777
Load one page, and there is a row.

53
00:03:05,777 --> 00:03:11,328
Wagtail creates it the first time something reads it, using your defaults.

54
00:03:11,328 --> 00:03:15,378
Which is why the studio name needs a sensible default.

55
00:03:15,378 --> 00:03:20,854
It is what the header shows before anyone has opened the settings screen.

56
00:03:21,654 --> 00:03:26,539
In a template it is settings, then the app label, then the model name,

57
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,586
then the field.

58
00:03:27,586 --> 00:03:32,332
The brand, the email as a mail to link, and the phone as a tel link,

59
00:03:32,332 --> 00:03:35,472
with the spaces cut out so it actually dials.

60
00:03:36,272 --> 00:03:37,526
And here it is.

61
00:03:37,526 --> 00:03:42,962
Reading a post, and the journal is still highlighted in the menu.

62
00:03:43,762 --> 00:03:44,845
And the footer.

63
00:03:44,845 --> 00:03:49,974
The name, the email, the phone number, the address and the social link.

64
00:03:49,974 --> 00:03:52,935
All of it comes from the settings screen,

65
00:03:52,935 --> 00:03:56,980
and the client can change any of it without calling you.

66
00:03:57,780 --> 00:04:00,294
Commit, and tag.

67
00:04:01,094 --> 00:04:02,804
Next episode, forms.

68
00:04:02,804 --> 00:04:09,560
A contact page that emails the studio, and keeps every submission in the admin.

69
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:14,960
Next episode, forms.

70
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:19,560
Thanks for watching.
